      "body": "## Summary\n\nRestore native NVIDIA report parity: human-readable Tier 3 baseline comparisons, visible tool versions, the original header scale, and Harbor logs/analysis in the Tier 3 card and Overview. Preserve concise summaries, one full Insights owner and folded provenance.\n\nAll report entry points retain one renderer. The [port manifest](https://github.com/NVIDIA/SkillEvaluator/blob/codex/report-gitlab-parity/docs/report-presentation-port.json) records the source and adaptations.\n\n## BEFORE / AFTER behavior\n\n| Area | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Header and versions | Compact overrides shrink branding; versions are hidden or disappear without a timestamp. | Renderer version beside the native-sized SkillEvaluator name, recorded SkillSpector versions inside Tier 1, and an aligned 1280px desktop layout. Long scanner versions wrap on mobile; print sizing stays unchanged. |\n| Overview comparison | Incomplete runs can lose the table; split views omit Overall, peer evidence or partial-comparison context. | One default-open Score/Baseline/Lift table with Overall and other-agent columns. Missing measurements remain N/A; custom-only runs show recorded custom metrics. |\n| Agent summaries | Native scorecards are missing; best/weakest dimension labels fail to populate. | Clickable per-agent scores, lift, trials and coverage. Recorded zero stays distinct from missing data; extrema use existing numeric measurements. |\n| Harbor | Actions appear only in Diagnostics; empty primary metadata can mask valid summary links. | Recorded logs and analysis actions in the Tier 3 card and Overview, including raw upload records and saved-run reconstruction. Per-job live metadata retains precedence; canonical downloads are unchanged. Local retained jobs require published URLs for hosted links. |\n| Insights | Long failure paragraphs and feedback repeat across surfaces. | Concise coverage/action in Overview; complete recorded cards once in Insights and full errors in Diagnostics. Distinct authored problems and evidence associations survive deduplication. |\n| Evidence and readability | Inconsistent styling, repeated open inventories and skill-specific plugin headings add clutter. | Shared native typography, palette, cards and tables; evidence integrated into its tier, passive provenance folded, and generic Dataset headings with the correct subject. |\n| Trials and resources | Native token/latency detail is incompletely surfaced. | Bounded recorded breakdowns, both-condition token charts and existing public resource tables, with accounting and omission notices. |\n| Downloads and interactions | Display-shaped exports and folded-content navigation have gaps. | Exact retained Tier 3 downloads; existing snapshot and CI artifact-link contracts preserved. Search, deep links, keyboard controls, print, no-JS and offline charts retain evidence access. |\n\n## Data preservation and scope\n\n- Presentation does not change scores, gates, applicability, coverage, backends or CLI options. Baseline-only, skipped and never-activated states cannot revive cached causal lift.\n- Retained replay preserves **218 result rows**, another **26 successful reference rows**, canonical payloads, plugin projections and original verdict/null/empty fields. Coverage stays **28/36** and **12/20**, with **zero provider calls or rescored trials**.\n- The supplied incomplete runs have no authoritative quality scores or recorded Harbor URLs. Their reports explain unavailable values; successful retained fixtures exercise the populated native views.\n- Preserve Chart.js 4.5.1 and notices, escaping/redaction, safe URLs, finite numeric validation, payload bounds and atomic output protections.\n- Private reports, reference payloads, screenshots and local audit artifacts are excluded from commits and distributions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] **3,736 reporting, producer, CI and upstream integration regression tests passed** on the final revision.\n- [x] **72 offline Chromium checks passed** from an installed wheel outside the checkout, including both Harbor link locations, raw upload records, canonical downloads, header/version placement, long scanner versions, mobile, print and no-JavaScript behavior.\n- [x] Wheel/sdist build, Ruff and pinned Fern validation; Fern reports zero errors and one optional authenticated-check warning.\n- [x] All **50 reporting files, the modified Tier 3 producer, and three license files** match source/wheel/sdist; source and both archives pass OSS boundary scans.\n- [x] Offline retained replay preserves **218 actual rows and 26 successful reference rows**, exact canonical data/plugin evidence, and coverage of **28/36** and **12/20**, with zero provider calls or rescored trials.\n- [x] **20 targeted desktop/mobile captures** cover before/after views and explicitly synthetic published-link examples, with source/image hashes and no browser, remote-network or page-overflow findings.\n- [x] No private reports, screenshots, reference payloads, credentials or proprietary benchmark content added to commits or distributions.\n\nAll PR commits carry the required DCO sign-offs. PR checks report the current whole-repository CI status.\n\n## Release Impact\n\n- [x] Updated `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- Changes the default HTML presentation and native feature visibility. The presentation changes introduce no scoring-policy, backend, CLI or canonical JSON schema migration.\n",
