      "body": "SkillSpector's default model on Anthropic and Bedrock was Claude Opus 5 while the chat default is Claude Opus 5.5. The docs explained it: SkillSpector 2.13.3 did not return structured output for Claude 5.5 models. We now pin 2.13.4, and that limitation is gone.\n\nChecked with an Anthropic API key, `SKILLSPECTOR_PROVIDER=anthropic`:\n- `skillspector scan skills/skillevaluator` with `claude-opus-5-5`: complete, 100% coverage, 43 calls, 0 retries, no `StructuredOutputParseError`.\n- `skillevaluator validate skills/skillevaluator --tiers 1 --llm` with `SKILL_EVAL_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic` and no model set: 10/10 checks passed, security complete.\n\nAlso checked through an OpenAI-compatible gateway serving the same model: 100% coverage. Bedrock was not exercised (no AWS credentials); it uses the same model generation and the same SkillSpector release.\n\n`SKILLSPECTOR_DEFAULT_MODELS` moves `anthropic` to `claude-opus-5-5` and `bedrock` to `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`. OpenAI already matched. The refusal fallback stays `claude-opus-4-8`, since it must differ from the judge model. Docs and tests follow; changelog entry added.\nCloses #608\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n\n---\n\n<a href=\"https://nvidia-cloud.devinenterprise.com/review/nvidia/skillevaluator/pull/607\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->\n",
