      "body": "SkillSpector's default model on the Anthropic and Bedrock providers is still Claude Opus 5, while the chat default is Claude Opus 5.5. The docs explain why: SkillSpector 2.13.3 did not return structured output for Claude 5.5 models.\n\nWe now pin SkillSpector 2.13.4, and that limitation is gone. A scan on the native Anthropic API with `claude-opus-5-5` completed at full coverage with no structured-output errors, and `skillevaluator validate skills/skillevaluator --tiers 1 --llm` passed 10/10 on the Anthropic provider.\n\nExpected: `SKILLSPECTOR_DEFAULT_MODELS` uses `claude-opus-5-5` for `anthropic` and `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5` for `bedrock`, and the docs stop saying Claude 5.5 is unsupported.\n",
