      "body": "The README's **Get started** section now shows the three ways in as illustrated columns, each with the command to run.\n\n- Three columns, each with a small card: run the CLI directly, add it to your repo via CI, wire it to your agent.\n- Column 1 shows `pip install skillevaluator` **or** `uv tool install skillevaluator`, then `skillevaluator validate ./my-skill --tiers 1`.\n- Each column links to its guide on docs.nvidia.com. That replaces the \"Guides:\" line under the table.\n- Long commands wrap with `\\` so no column needs a scroll bar. The README is 1,098 words, under the 1,100-word cap.\n\n**Merge order**\n\nDraft until #610 merges. Column 3 links to the agent guide, and #610 is the rewrite of that page, so the guide goes first. The agent guide changes that were in this PR moved to #610.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `pytest tests/test_oss_packaging.py` (50 passed) and `ruff check src tests`.\n- Rendered the README locally with GitHub's stylesheet at the repository page width to check the columns and the wrapped commands.\n\n**Follow-up**\n\nThe three card images use repo-relative paths, so they render on GitHub but not on the PyPI project page. They need pinned absolute URLs, like the wordmark, before the next release.\n",
