      },
      "body": "The \"Evaluate Skills from Your Agent\" page now leads with what to run and shows what happens, so a first-time reader can set it up without reading the whole page.\n\n- Starts with `npx skills add NVIDIA/SkillEvaluator`, with Claude Code and Codex examples and where the skill lands for each. A collapsed section covers readers without npx.\n- Then the two ways to call the skill (just ask, or by name), an example session and a how-it-works diagram.\n- Installing the CLI yourself, provider keys, live evaluation and sandbox notes moved into collapsed sections.\n\n**Merge order**\n\nThe page says the agent installs the CLI when it is missing. That matches #570, so this should land after it. #601 adds a paragraph to the same page, so whichever of the two lands second needs a small merge. The README change in #609 follows this one.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `npx skills add NVIDIA/SkillEvaluator -a claude-code -y` and `-a codex -y`, each run in an empty folder: the skill lands in `.claude/skills/skillevaluator` and `.agents/skills/skillevaluator`.\n- The example session's command and numbers come from a real `skillevaluator tier1 ./my-skill --no-llm` run on a small sample skill.\n- `pytest tests/test_oss_packaging.py tests/reporting/test_tier3_completed_agent_docs.py` (59 passed), `ruff check src tests` and `fern check` (0 errors).\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n\n---\n\n<a href=\"https://nvidia-cloud.devinenterprise.com/review/nvidia/skillevaluator/pull/610\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->",
